WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:06.710
In September 1978, Bulgarian writer and dissident
Georgi Markov was living in London and working

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:08.349
for the BBC.

00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:13.019
Almost ten years earlier, he had defected
from his country and been deemed a traitor

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:19.260
to Bulgaria, which was ruled by an authoritarian
government behind the Iron Curtain.

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:23.640
One day on his way to work, Markov felt a
sudden pain in his leg.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.850
It seemed that a passerby had hit him with
the tip of their umbrella.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:33.180
But over the next few hours, it became clear
that this was no accident.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:39.480
Markov proceeded to experience fever, muscle
pain, swollen lymph nodes, and heart problems.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:43.750
He was admitted to the hospital, but within
four days, he was dead.

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.750
[1]

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.020
When medical experts conducted an autopsy,
they realized the jab with the umbrella had

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:54.570
administered a deadly toxin directly into
Markov’s muscle - a toxin produced from

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.320
one of the world’s most deadly plants.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.899
There are many dangerous plants in the world.

00:01:00.899 --> 00:01:05.510
There’s the manchineel tree that grows in
the tropical regions of North and South America,

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:11.960
and which is so toxic that if you stand under
it during a rainstorm, your skin will blister.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:17.600
A tree that grows in Southeast Asia, the pong-pong,
is sometimes called the “suicide tree”

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.140
because of the toxicity of its fruit.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.640
In the southwestern Indian state of Kerala,
fruit from this tree is responsible for 50%

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.790
of all plant poisonings, and is thought to
have killed more than 500 people between 1989

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.790
and 1999 alone.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.790
[2]

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.960
Even tobacco is a deadly plant, considering
how many millions of people die each year

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.820
of illnesses related to smoking.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.110
But there are two plants in particular that
have been used by spies, murderers, and assassins

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:52.759
for thousands of years—the castor bean plant
and the deadly nightshade.

00:01:52.759 --> 00:01:57.250
Both of them are so toxic that eating just
a handful of their berries or seeds would

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.619
be enough to kill an adult within a couple
days.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:05.729
And yet the very chemicals that make deadly
nightshade and castor bean plants so dangerous

00:02:05.729 --> 00:02:09.700
have also been found to contain valuable pharmacological
properties.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:15.910
They’re used in everything from cancer treatments
to antidotes to deadly nerve gasses.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.370
What makes these plants so unbelievably deadly?

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:24.200
And how on earth did we figure out the positive
side effects of these deadly shrubs without

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.620
causing a lot of accidental poisonings?

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:37.500
Ricin is one of the most toxic compounds produced
by plants and has been used in everything

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.739
from political assassinations, like in the
umbrella assassination, to fictional narratives

00:02:42.739 --> 00:02:44.670
like “Breaking Bad.”

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:49.121
Thanks to the ubiquity of the shrub that it
comes from, the castor bean plant, ricin is

00:02:49.121 --> 00:03:04.980
also one of the most common biological agents
used 

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.470
in biocrimes.

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:16.459
What’s most remarkable about the plant are
its seeds, which are commonly called “beans.”

00:03:16.459 --> 00:03:24.040
A large plant can produce 150,000 seeds every
season and they contain a valuable commodity

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:26.680
as well as a deadly poison.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:31.810
Each seed is about 50% oil, which has been
used for fuel and as medicine.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:38.730
But the seeds also contain ricin, a poison
so deadly that it only takes 3 to 6 to kill

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:39.730
an adult.

00:03:39.730 --> 00:03:40.730
[3]

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:46.010
Ricin is one of the most poisonous naturally-occurring
substances known, but how quickly it kills

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:51.069
someone, and how it affects the body, depends
largely on the way it’s administered.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:52.069
[4]

00:03:52.069 --> 00:03:57.370
Inhaling ricin and having it injected into
the muscle are far more dangerous than ingesting

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.370
it.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:04.129
The lethal dose for inhalation of ricin is
3-5mcg/kg (LD50 0.003 mg/kg) whereas the lethal

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:07.640
dose for oral consumption is 20mg/kg.

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:14.670
This is because ricin works by inactivating
ribosomes, which are structures made of RNA

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.430
and proteins that create all the proteins
necessary for cells to function.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:26.570
Without ribosomes, cells die—and ricin causes
cell death on a massive scale.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:33.360
One molecule of ricin toxin can inactivate
1500 to 2000 ribosomes per minute.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:34.360
[5]

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.800
When ricin enters the body, it affects whichever
organ systems are closest.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:44.090
That means if it’s inhaled, it destroys
lung tissue, causing fluid buildup, alveolar

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.960
inflammation, and necrotizing pneumonia.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.270
Basically, your lungs are destroyed and you
die.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:56.210
And ricin powder attacks have been attempted
at least twice that we know of, with envelopes

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:02.770
containing ricin being sent to the US Senate
in 2004 and President Obama in 2013.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:03.800
[6]

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:09.030
Things aren’t much better if you ingest
ricin: you’ll have stomach cramps, vomiting,

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:13.850
diarrhea, ulcers along your GI tract, and
possible renal failure.

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:19.430
But because doctors can treat those symptoms
in the hospital, you still might survive.

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:24.340
Would-be murderers in the US, the UK, and
Germany have all been arrested for attempting

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:30.740
to extract ricin, and the FBI will even investigate
Americans simply for planting castor beans

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:42.750
on their property.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:46.040
Even processing the seeds for oil can come
with dangers.

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:51.430
A manufacturing plant in Brazil, one of the
main producers of castor oil, reported more

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:56.840
than 150 cases of bronchial asthma, including
nine deaths.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:01.130
When health officials investigated the incident,
they found that processing methods of the

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:03.490
castor bean had sickened the workers.

00:06:03.490 --> 00:06:04.490
[7]

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.640
Given how deadly ricin is, it should come
as no surprise that plenty of countries have

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.840
investigated its use as a chemical weapon.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:16.199
The United States War Department researched
whether it could be used as a toxic dust to

00:06:16.199 --> 00:06:21.240
spray on the battlefield, or to coat bullets
and shrapnel with, during WWI.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:26.889
But ricin is unstable under heat, limiting
its use in shells.

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:32.539
And even though the US conducted more tests
on ricin during WWII, it was ultimately never

00:06:32.539 --> 00:06:33.539
deployed.

00:06:33.539 --> 00:06:34.539
[8]

00:06:34.539 --> 00:06:38.830
Treaties on the use of bacteriological and
toxin weapons later prohibited the use of

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:42.520
ricin–but that doesn’t mean governments
haven’t tried.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:47.910
In the 1980s, Iraq aerosolized ricin and tested
it in animal experiments, though they never

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:49.720
used it for warfare.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:55.310
But ricin is much less toxic than botulinum
and anthrax, so it’s not actually as useful

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.479
for mass murder.

00:06:56.479 --> 00:07:02.470
That’s why it’s become one of the poisons
of choice for political assassinations.

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:07.680
But another plant lurks in the forests of
Europe, its berries dark, delicious, and even

00:07:07.680 --> 00:07:10.860
more deadly.

00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:19.150
Atropa belladonna, sometimes known as the
deadly nightshade, belongs to same family

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:23.680
as plenty of our edible favorites, like tomatoes,
potatoes, and peppers.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:28.181
But even though the purple berries of the
deadly nightshade are apparently sweet, they

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:31.680
are far from being safe for consumption.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:36.620
They contain multiple dangerous alkaloids,
including atropine and scopolamine, and have

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:40.450
a long history of being used in poisonings.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:43.550
Even their scientific name suggests how dangerous
they are.

00:07:43.550 --> 00:07:49.500
According to Greek mythology, the three Fates
were responsible for dictating human lives.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:55.889
Lachesis measured the thread of destiny at
birth, Clotho spun it, and Atropos ended life

00:07:55.889 --> 00:07:57.319
by cutting the thread.

00:07:57.319 --> 00:07:58.409
[9]

00:07:58.409 --> 00:08:03.699
Yet even though deadly nightshade was used
to murder Roman emperors and political rivals,

00:08:03.699 --> 00:08:06.060
it also had its place in medicine.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:12.310
Renaissance women put it in their eyes to
make their pupils larger–a practice ophthalmologists

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:14.599
still use today to dilate the eyes.

00:08:14.599 --> 00:08:20.630
It was used to bring on delirium and hallucinations,
including the famous “flying ointment”

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:25.690
made by witches, and helped in treating pain
from childbirth. [10]

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:31.000
Clearly, even before the discovery of organic
chemistry, humans understood something crucial

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:35.710
about these deadly plants: the dose makes
the poison.

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:41.659
While castor beans deliver all their toxicity
with one chemical punch in the form of ricin,

00:08:41.659 --> 00:08:46.820
deadly nightshade includes more of a cocktail,
with the most potent toxins being atropine

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.560
and scopolamine.

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:52.360
Both act on neurotransmitters, and target
acetylcholine.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:57.529
Normally, this chemical carries messages between
the nervous system and the muscles.

00:08:57.529 --> 00:09:02.770
When it gets to the end of a synapse, it binds
to acetylcholine receptors, which play a variety

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:07.269
of roles, from regulating heart rate to stimulating
sweat glands.

00:09:07.269 --> 00:09:12.890
Atropine and scopolamine are acetylcholine
receptor antagonists—basically, they compete

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:17.399
with acetylcholine for access to that connection
between the nervous system and the rest of

00:09:17.399 --> 00:09:18.770
the body.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:23.870
When these toxins bind to the acetylcholine
receptors, they prevent acetylcholine from

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:29.070
transmitting messages between the nervous
system and the rest of our muscles and organs.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.970
And this causes a whole host of problems.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:32.970
[11]

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:36.279
The body’s temperature regulation is thrown
off, causing fever.

00:09:36.279 --> 00:09:41.970
The pupils of the eye dilate, sometimes to
such a degree that the iris is invisible.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:45.760
Salivation is suppressed, causing extreme
thirst.

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:50.360
And patients might exhibit delirium, hallucinations,
and seizures.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:55.950
The plant itself was famously used to poison
Roman emperors hundreds of years ago, and

00:09:55.950 --> 00:10:00.810
some scholars think it’s what gave Juliet
a death-like appearance at the end of Shakespeare’s

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:03.279
play “Romeo and Juliet.”

00:10:03.279 --> 00:10:09.089
But once the chemical atropine was isolated
in 1830, that by itself became more commonly

00:10:09.089 --> 00:10:11.280
used in poisonings.

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:16.200
One of the most bizarre episodes happened
in the UK in 1994.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:21.490
Biologist Paul Agutter was able to get atropine
from his university’s toxicology lab and

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:24.170
use it to poison his wife.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:28.459
Because the chemical is extremely bitter,
he dosed multiple bottles of tonic water with

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:34.230
the poison, leaving some of the bottles at
a supermarket to cover his tracks and bringing

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.089
the most heavily dosed bottle home to make
his wife a gin and tonic.

00:10:39.089 --> 00:10:44.399
Multiple people fell ill with atropine poisoning,
but none had a dose as high as Agutter’s

00:10:44.399 --> 00:10:45.399
wife.

00:10:45.399 --> 00:10:49.350
Fortunately, her gin and tonic was so bitter
that she drank only half of the cocktail,

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:51.110
and was able to survive.

00:10:51.110 --> 00:10:52.110
[12]

00:10:52.110 --> 00:10:56.490
This kind of poisoning is rare, since atropine
is harder to isolate from deadly nightshade

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.220
than ricin is from castor beans.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:02.940
But the other chemical in the plant, scopolamine,
has had a growing reputation as a dangerous

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:07.640
poison because it’s used in robberies and
sexual assault.

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:13.050
After the victim is dosed, they become highly
suggestible and often suffer amnesia after

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:16.970
the event–making it much easier for the
criminal to get away.

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:17.970
[13]

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:22.100
But, surprisingly, the properties of both
the castor bean plant and deadly nightshade

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:30.149
that make them so dangerous can be harnessed
by us in a way that turns them from poison,

00:11:30.149 --> 00:11:36.139
to panacea.

00:11:36.139 --> 00:11:40.800
Although deadly nightshade and the castor
bean plant are very dangerous, they both also

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.740
play a big role in medicine and other industries.

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:49.209
Castor bean especially is a valuable commodity,
thanks to its oil.

00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:55.960
Soybeans have 15 to 20 % oil, and sunflower
seeds have 25 to 35% oil, whereas castor beans

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.730
have 40 to 55% oil.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.730
[14]

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:04.060
And the chemical properties of the oil mean
its viscosity doesn’t change much with higher

00:12:04.060 --> 00:12:08.430
temperatures, so it is especially good at
lubricating hot metal.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:12.750
It’s one of the best oils for racing and
jet turbine engines.

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:18.370
What’s more, researchers have found that
castor oil could be an excellent biodiesel,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:22.820
even more effective than plants like corn
and soybeans, and the plant is hardy enough

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:27.260
to be used in bioremediation, to clean up
soil that’s been contaminated with heavy

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:29.470
metals like copper and lead.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.470
[15]

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:35.329
Deadly nightshade also has a role to play
in medicine, both with common ailments and

00:12:35.329 --> 00:12:37.310
in more extreme cases.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:42.550
Atropine and scopolamine have all been modified
to treat asthma, motion sickness, provide

00:12:42.550 --> 00:12:48.269
sedation and pain relief during childbirth,
treat Parkinson’s disease, and as an antipsychotic

00:12:48.269 --> 00:12:49.500
drug.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:55.500
And atropine has one particularly surprising
function: it’s an antidote to nerve gas

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.830
poisoning.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:13:03.279
In a healthy individual, acetylcholine’s
action is stopped by an enzyme called acetylcholinesterase.

00:13:03.279 --> 00:13:07.180
This keeps acetylcholine levels regulated
and in a healthy balance.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:12.290
But nerve gasses like sarin, soman, and VX
binds to the enzyme, and blocks its action.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:18.520
Therefore, acetylcholine builds up out of
control, binding to the receptors unchecked.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:23.190
This causes excessive production of fluids,
vomiting, difficulty breathing, and heart

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:24.560
problems.

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:27.269
But atropine can work to fix this.

00:13:27.269 --> 00:13:33.149
Because atropine blocks acetylcholine receptors,
it counteracts the effects of nerve agents.

00:13:33.149 --> 00:13:38.959
Even if a lot of acetylcholine builds up between
cells, it can’t actually make the connection.

00:13:38.959 --> 00:13:39.959
[16]

00:13:39.959 --> 00:13:44.620
So while nerve agents are extremely lethal,
they can be countered by a dose of atropine

00:13:44.620 --> 00:13:48.339
quickly administered—just like Nicholas
Cage’s character does in “The Rock”

00:13:48.339 --> 00:13:50.580
after being exposed by nerve gas.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:53.470
That said, its a very tricky balance.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:58.579
There’s a possibility of atropine poisoning
if you take too much as an antidote, or take

00:13:58.579 --> 00:14:01.130
it without being exposed to nerve gas.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:07.209
Duri ng the Gulf War, atropine auto-injectors
were distributed across Israel in case of

00:14:07.209 --> 00:14:13.660
a gas attack, and nearly 300 cases of children
accidentally poisoning themselves were reported.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:16.639
Luckily, there were no fatalities. [17]

00:14:16.639 --> 00:14:22.140
All this is to say that both these plants
can still be dangerous, even when put to helpful

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:23.370
purposes.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:28.170
And plenty of people get poisoned just from
consuming the berries or seeds of the two

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:33.010
plants, so remember to never, ever eat something
on a trail if you are not 100 % confident

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.490
you know what it is, and that it’s safe.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:39.130
Learning what these plants look like is the
best way to avoid stupidly dying.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:44.890
In fact, learning in general evolved as a
concept so we can avoid stupidly dying.

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:47.899
And we can even use learning for other things
too.

00:14:47.899 --> 00:14:53.449
I personally, have dabbled in learning from
time to time, and find that life does improve

00:14:53.449 --> 00:14:55.690
when I dust off some neurons.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:59.449
It helps me in my work, it helps me to gain
confidence, and it helps me to feel a part

00:14:59.449 --> 00:15:02.230
of the big, scary, complicated world that
we live in.

